class.description:
An [InputIconSet] assigns a [Texture2D] to each [enum Key], [enum MouseButton], [enum JoyButton] and gamepad axis direction, plus one fallback icon per event type. Use it for in-game button prompts, and register it in [InputIconServer] (or in the project settings [code]input_devices/icons/*[/code]) so the editor's Input Map shows the icons too.
In the Inspector, every value has its own property, grouped as [b]Keyboard[/b], [b]Mouse[/b], [b]Gamepad Buttons[/b] and [b]Gamepad Axes[/b]. The icons are saved in [member key_icons], [member mouse_button_icons], [member joy_button_icons] and [member joy_axis_icons], keyed by the text names of [method InputAction.event_to_text] ([code]"Space"[/code], [code]"Left"[/code], [code]"LeftStickPress"[/code], [code]"LeftStickLeft"[/code]).
[codeblocks]
[gdscript]
var icons = InputIconSet.new()
icons.set_key_icon(KEY_SPACE, preload("res://prompts/space.png"))
icons.set_joy_button_icon(JOY_BUTTON_A, preload("res://prompts/a.png"))
icons.set_joy_axis_icon(JOY_AXIS_LEFT_X, -1.0, preload("res://prompts/left_stick_left.png"))
var icon = icons.get_icon_for_text("Gamepad:A")
[/gdscript]
[csharp]
var icons = new InputIconSet();
icons.SetKeyIcon(Key.Space, GD.Load<Texture2D>("res://prompts/space.png"));
icons.SetJoyButtonIcon(JoyButton.A, GD.Load<Texture2D>("res://prompts/a.png"));
icons.SetJoyAxisIcon(JoyAxis.LeftX, -1.0f, GD.Load<Texture2D>("res://prompts/left_stick_left.png"));
Texture2D icon = icons.GetIconForText("Gamepad:A");
[/csharp]
[/codeblocks]
